{"repositoryId":1158120471,"availability":"available","full":"dgerrells/chartai","name":"chartai","description":"Not just any javasript chart library MY chart library. ","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":26,"forks":0,"created":"2026-02-14T20:39:42Z","updated":"2026-03-10T07:10:28Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://dgerrells.github.io/chartai/demo/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.265Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.265Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.265Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.265Z","stars":26,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Are you looking for a simple tiny little chart library which can draw as many lines and points as you have vram? Look no further.","chartai is a library that can draw millions and millions of lines across thousands of series wickedly fast. It uses a passive rendering system that only update charts when needed. It lives in a web worker keeping the main thread free. It is fully pluggable so you only take way you need or add what's missing.","This library was inspired by uplot which is likely all you need. But if you do need the performance without the bundle bloat, this may do it. With all the core charts and plugins, chartai is about the same size as uplot."],"features":["Silly overly complicated demo","Tiny, unlimited line charts at 11kb","Customizable with plugins","Lines, scatter, bar, and candlestick out of the box","Chart synchronization"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dgerrells/chartai/blob/main/readme.md","fingerprint":"ff695f7cff43b9127cebe368262a629a5b3899d838d69ceec6c23637854ac31e","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.553Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.553Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Are you looking for a simple tiny little chart library which can draw as many lines and points as you have vram? Look no further.","sou